---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { prompts, categories } from '../data/prompts';

const a = SITE.author;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: `About ${SITE.name}`,
  url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
};
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.name}: who writes the prompts, how each page is built and how to report an error.`}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="narrow article-head prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>

    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a free library of AI prompts for people who want to understand what they paste into a chat box.
      Today it holds {prompts.length} prompts across {categories.length} categories, and it grows as new ones are written and reviewed.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
    <p>
      I am {a.name}, {a.role}, based in {a.country}. {a.story}
    </p>

    <h2>How a prompt page is built</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>I start from a real task, such as summarizing a report, planning a content cluster or tuning a query.</li>
      <li>I write the prompt with named variables so it is clear what you are meant to change.</li>
      <li>I try it on sample material with {a.models} and rewrite it until the structure of the result is reliable.</li>
      <li>I add a worked example, variations for other situations and the mistakes I would warn a colleague about.</li>
      <li>I show a "last reviewed" date and revisit pages when tools change.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is not a copy of other prompt lists, and it does not promise guaranteed results. AI output can be wrong, incomplete or out of date, so
      every page encourages you to check facts, numbers and code before you rely on them.
    </p>

    <h2>Free to use, supported by ads</h2>
    <p>
      The prompts are free to use. The site may show advertising to cover running costs. Ads do not influence what is written, and
      the way advertising and cookies work is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and requests</h2>
    <p>
      If you find a mistake or want a prompt for a task that is missing, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Corrections are made on the page and the review date is updated.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
